  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.678 accuracy. The evidence shows that (1) scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder, (2) avgpool outperforms transformer aggregation, (3) weighted fusion beats concat, and (4) adding image with weighted fusion gives a modest boost over RNA-only (0.678 vs 0.650). The image modality contributed ~0.028 improvement with resnet50, but image-only resnet50 was very weak (0.21), suggesting the image encoder quality is a bottleneck. config_037 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l (a substantially stronger pretrained backbone), keeping all other settings identical to the current best. This is a clean single-variable test that isolates whether a stronger image representation can further improve the weighted multimodal fusion. With only 1 experiment remaining, exploiting the proven best configuration while testing the most impactful unexplored variable (image encoder strength) is the highest-value use of the final budget slot."
